# <WORKSPACE_NAME> — Workspace Router

> **Identity.** A multi-repo workspace (framework Chapter 13): <N> independently deployed repos —
> <REPO_LIST> — cloned under this directory (gitignored; `workspace.json` is the source of truth;
> `<WORKSPACE_SLUG>.code-workspace` opens them together). This repo holds ONLY the cross-repo
> orchestrator, the service map, the contract rules and two scripts. No CI; deploys nothing.
>
> **Single-repo work does not belong here.** Open the repo and use its own orchestrator.

## Golden rules (always)

1. **The workspace writes to a child only through that child's own orchestrator** — via
   `scripts/delegate.sh` (the child's own CLI session, its hooks fire) or, interactively, by
   invoking `<repo>-orchestrator` as a subagent. Never edit a child's files from a workspace turn.
2. **Producer first, additive only, deployed before consumers** —
   `.github/instructions/cross-repo-contracts.instructions.md`.
3. **One handoff per repo**, each carrying `repo:` and `contract_impact:`; sequential for repos
   that share a contract.
4. **Invoke child ORCHESTRATORS by name, never child specialists** — specialist names collide
   across folders.
5. **No evidence, no claim** — cross-repo claims cite `<repo>:<path>:<line>`.
6. **Production approvals are per repo, per incident, current turn.** Nothing here approves anything.
7. **The cloud agent is per repo.** A cross-repo change is one task per repo, in contract order.

## Routing

| Task | Use |
|---|---|
| Touches more than one repo / a contract with consumers elsewhere | `<WORKSPACE_SLUG>-orchestrator` |
| "Is this contract change safe? who reads this field?" | `contract-guardian` (REVIEW-ONLY) |
| "Which repo owns X?" / the map is stale | `service-mapper` |
| Run a child's orchestrator from a script | `/delegate <repo> <handoff-file>` |
| Anything inside one repo | that repo's own orchestrator — leave the workspace |

